Student Record Management System Using C

A Student Record Management System developed using the C programming language and Linked List data structure. This project is designed to efficiently store, manage, search, update, and delete student records.

Features

- Add new student records
- Display all student records
- Search for a student using their details
- Update existing student information
- Delete student records
- Dynamic memory allocation using linked lists
- Menu-driven and user-friendly interface

Technologies Used

- Programming Language: C
- Data Structure: Singly Linked List
- Concepts: Structures, Pointers, Dynamic Memory Allocation, Functions, and File Handling

Objective

The main objective of this project is to demonstrate the practical implementation of data structures and C programming concepts by creating a simple and efficient system for managing student information.

Learning Outcomes

Through this project, we gain practical knowledge of:

- Structures in C
- Pointers and dynamic memory allocation
- Linked list operations
- User-defined functions
- Searching, insertion, deletion, and updating operations
- Menu-driven programming

This project is suitable for C programming, Data Structures, and Embedded Systems beginners to understand how linked lists can be used in a real-world application.
